ADDITIONAL PERMISSION — COMMERCIAL OUTPUT EXCEPTION

The licensor grants the following additional permission notwithstanding the
noncommercial-use limitation in the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0.

1. Commercial Use to Create Output

You may use the Software, including in a business, professional practice, or
other commercial activity, for the purpose of creating Output.

For example, you may use SashikoStudio to create designs or files for yourself,
for a client, for products you sell, or as part of a commercial design or
manufacturing workflow.

This permission applies to use of the Software to create Output. It does not
grant permission to commercialize the Software itself.

2. Output Rights

Subject to the Third-Party Rights section below, you may use, copy, modify,
distribute, publish, sublicense, manufacture from, and sell Output for any
purpose, including commercial purposes, without payment of royalties or a
requirement to attribute SashikoStudio.

You may also use Output to make, distribute, and sell physical products,
including stitched works, printed templates, guides, tools, patterns, and
3D-printed objects.

To the extent that any copyright or other intellectual-property rights
controlled by the licensor are embodied in Output, the licensor grants you a
worldwide, perpetual, irrevocable, royalty-free license to exercise those
rights as necessary for the permissions above.

3. Definition of Output

"Output" means a design, pattern, file, document, model, image, measurement,
toolpath, or other result produced through the ordinary use of the Software.

Output includes, without limitation, exported SVG, STL, PDF, image, pattern,
template, and similar files.

Output does not include:

(a) the Software itself;
(b) the Software's source code or object code;
(c) a copy or substantial portion of the Software's user interface;
(d) documentation or other repository contents copied independently of an
    Output; or
(e) source assets distributed with the Software except to the extent those
    assets are represented or incorporated in an Output produced through
    ordinary use of the Software.

4. No Commercialization of the Software

The Additional Permission does not permit you to use the Software itself as a
commercial product or service.

Without a separate commercial license from the licensor, you may not:

(a) sell, rent, lease, license, or sublicense the Software or a modified version
    of the Software;

(b) commercially redistribute, repackage, rebrand, or white-label the Software
    or a modified version of the Software;

(c) incorporate the Software's source code or object code into a product or
    service that is sold, licensed, monetized, or otherwise provided for
    commercial advantage;

(d) charge users for access to the Software or to a hosted, embedded, or
    modified version of the Software;

(e) operate an advertising-supported, sponsored, subscription-based, or
    otherwise monetized service whose product includes access to or use of the
    Software; or

(f) distribute a modified version of the Software for a commercial purpose.

For clarity, charging for Output, for physical goods made from Output, or for
design services in which you use the Software to create Output is expressly
permitted and is not considered commercialization of the Software under this
section.

5. Noncommercial Software Uses

Nothing in this Additional Permission reduces the permissions already granted
by the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0. Noncommercial use, modification,
and distribution of the Software remain governed by that license.

6. Third-Party Rights

These terms grant only rights that the licensor has authority to grant. They do
not grant rights in third-party fonts, libraries, trademarks, imported artwork,
user-supplied content, or other third-party materials that may be used with or
included in the Software or an Output. Those materials remain subject to their
applicable terms and rights.

7. No Claim to User Content

The licensor does not claim ownership of content that you create or import
merely because you use the Software. The permissions in this license concern
only rights controlled by the licensor.

8. Conflict

If this Additional Permission conflicts with the PolyForm Noncommercial License
1.0.0, this Additional Permission controls only to the extent necessary to
permit the activities expressly described above. All other terms of the
PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 remain in effect.

9. Separate Commercial Licensing

The licensor may offer separate commercial licenses for uses of the Software
